      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://nostr.how/en/guides/get-verified&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;nip-05&lt;/a&gt; is a convenience for identifying users on nostr such as &lt;code&gt;mordaunt@jackmordaunt.com&lt;/code&gt;, which is&#xA;shorter and more memorable than a &lt;span class=&#34;tooltip&#34;&gt;&#xA;  raw npub&#xA;  &lt;span class=&#34;tooltiptext&#34;&gt;npub14l0387z0ejfmnn3j38nnalg5p57952d84aqakqguhzx7p7pns2vqg3x78w&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It works by making a &lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt; request at &lt;code&gt;jackmordaunt.com/.well-known/nostr.json&lt;/code&gt; and extracting the&#xA;public keys from the JSON response.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This quick guide will show you how to host your own with a Hugo site.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;add-your-configuration&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Add your configuration.&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#add-your-configuration&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Inside your &lt;code&gt;hugo.toml&lt;/code&gt;, add:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
